jobs.description:
Are you looking for a stable job with fixed working hours and a reliable employer? Do you enjoy physical work and working together with colleagues? Then we have a great opportunity for you!
FunctieomschrijvingFor our client, we are looking for motivated Order Pickers to join a modern logistics team. Experience is welcome, but if you are motivated and willing to learn, we would also like to meet you.
As an Order Picker, you play an important role in the warehouse. Every day you make sure customer orders are picked correctly and prepared for delivery. Accuracy is important because customers depend on receiving the right products.
Your daily tasks include:
- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking products for quality and quantity;
- Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
- Making sure labels and orders are correct;
- Keeping your workplace clean, safe, and organised;
- Working together with your team to meet daily targets.

The work is active, so you'll be on your feet for most of the day. If you enjoy staying busy instead of sitting behind a desk, this job is a great fit.
Functie-eisenWe are looking for someone who:
- Speaks English, Polish and/or Dutch;
- Works accurately and pays attention to detail;
- Enjoys physical work;
- Can work independently as well as in a team;
- Is willing to work in a chilled warehouse environment;
- Is available to work Monday through Saturday. Working on Sundays and public holidays may also be part of the schedule;
- Has experience with order picking or a handheld scanner (preferred, but not required).

Arbeidsvoorwaarden- A starting salary of €2,600 gross per month (based on full-time employment);
- Shift allowance where applicable;
- Travel allowance;
- A good pension scheme;
- Stable working hours;
- A pleasant and international working environment;
- A reliable employer with long-term opportunities;
- The chance to develop yourself and grow within the company.

BedrijfsomschrijvingYour new employer produces

For our client in Amsterdam, we are looking for a key account manager (B2B retail) for the German market. Together with your colleagues from the sales team, you will continue to sell a large assortment of cool, practical, and sustainable products. In this position, you are responsible for expanding the customer base and maintaining the current relationships. Your base location will be our NL office; they prefer that you visit your customers in Germany as much as possible to strengthen the relationship and introduce the newest items. The ratio of new client acquisition to existing client management is 50/50.
Responsibilities: - Develop and maintain strong relationships with key accounts in Germany;
- Identify new business opportunities and drive sales growth;
- Negotiate contracts and agreements with clients;
- Provide excellent customer service and support.
- Collaborate with internal teams to meet customer needs;
- Prepare and deliver sales presentations to potential clients;
- Monitor market trends and competitor activities;
- Meet sales targets and objectives;
- Travel within Germany for client meetings and business development.

RequirementsYou know how to find commercial opportunities, and with your strong drive plus a good dose of perseverance and guts, you grab them. Besides:- Commercially driven;
- Positive, enthusiastic, and friendly;
- Experience in sales or account management for a minimum of 7 years and having worked with key accounts for several years; 
- Business fluent in German (C2 level) and English;
- Familiarity with the German retail / FMCG market and consumer trends is a MUST;
- excellent verbal and written communication abilities;
- Strong problem-solving skills and a proven track record of building and maintaining client relationships
- Living near the Amsterdam area (or have plans to relocate there very soon)

Benefits- 13th month bonus
- 8% holiday allowance
- A full-time (40 hour) contract; first contract is for 7 months.
- Fully onsite
